    {
      "id": "E9gLOa72xEm1FJjfFn9e1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2019.745661883671,
      "y": 5672.370134959594,
      "width": 739.2698113185659,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "KNS5n0fWJIHhRf6mcOM8j",
      "index": "a5zzzzt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 609075896,
      "version": 143,
      "versionNonce": 2038369224,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784685132412,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "8.4 The evolution of Flash Attention\nEach generation traded simplicity for percentage points of throughput. For\nproduction systems at scale, those percentage points translate to millions\nof dollars in hardware costs, making the complexity worthwhile.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "8.4 The evolution of Flash Attention\nEach generation traded simplicity for percentage points of throughput. For production systems at scale, those percentage points translate to millions of dollars in hardware costs, making the complexity worthwhile.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "tGlL9hJBN5phEhBIMiO_S",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2006.4845403302593,
      "y": 5800.608662526632,
      "width": 745.5242865184368,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "KNS5n0fWJIHhRf6mcOM8j",
      "index": "a5zzzzx",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 935088328,
      "version": 398,
      "versionNonce": 715027640,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784685132412,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Modern kernels are becoming asynchronous, pipelined, and warp-specialized.\nThe programming model is shifting from \"write a function that a thread\nexecutes\" to \"write a state machine where warps handle different pipeline\nstages.\" This is powerful but challenging, requiring new abstractions and\ntools. The CUDA ecosystem is responding with libraries like CUTLASS for\nTensor Core programming and domain-specific languages like Triton for\nsimpler kernel authorship.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Modern kernels are becoming asynchronous, pipelined, and warp-specialized. The programming model is shifting from \"write a function that a thread executes\" to \"write a state machine where warps handle different pipeline stages.\" This is powerful but challenging, requiring new abstractions and tools. The CUDA ecosystem is responding with libraries like CUTLASS for Tensor Core programming and domain-specific languages like Triton for simpler kernel authorship.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Isz9kdxTW2oRfFTofr9la",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1993.0244522514545,
      "y": 6015.435815572821,
      "width": 797.3679673599834,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "KNS5n0fWJIHhRf6mcOM8j",
      "index": "a5zzzzz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1710779064,
      "version": 250,
      "versionNonce": 742019784,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784685132412,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Flash Attention’s evolution from v1 to v4 shows a consistent pattern: each\ngeneration exploits more hardware-specific features (TMA, WGMMA, warp\nspecialization, FP8) for incremental speedups at increasing implementation\ncomplexity.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Flash Attention’s evolution from v1 to v4 shows a consistent pattern: each generation exploits more hardware-specific features (TMA, WGMMA, warp specialization, FP8) for incremental speedups at increasing implementation complexity.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KNS5n0fWJIHhRf6mcOM8j",
